    "abstract": "There have been considerable controversies concerning ego in modern philosophy between two intellectual groups, one of which attempts to remove transcendental ego from philosophy, the other of which attempts to transform transcendental ego into transcendental ego closely related with our concrete life. Husserl’s ego-theory,especially, personal ego-theory can be located historically at the very beginning of the latter intellectual groups. Husserl didn’t regard personal ego as pure and transcendental ego at the early stage of his inquiry until he found new phenomenological reduction, namely, phenomenological-psychological reduction. And at last he could develop personal identity-theory after he found habitconcept,which means mode of being of personal ego’s property According to Husserl, personal identity based on habit-concept is 1) identity closely related with intentional experience and intentional object, 2) identity constituted through historical genesis, and 3) identity depending on passive material. Thus Husserl’s personal ego is different from Descartes’ and Kant’s transcendental ego. And Husserl’s personal ego is different from empirical ego too, because only under idea of self-preservation personal ego can constitute his identity. In conclusion, my paper aims to show that Husserl’s personal ego can overcome the shortcomings of transcendental ego and empirical ego, and contribute to establish new ego-theory in modern philosophy.",
